23	/**
24	 * The claims on a sheet: added to a person and edited (amount, date, note). A claim given no date
25	 * takes the sheet's today. A claim starts as DRAFT and moves through its statuses (see
26	 * {@link ClaimStatus}); a change its status does not allow is refused. Only a DRAFT can be edited:
27	 * to change an open claim, void it and add a new one. Settling a claim fixes its
28	 * due at the rate its person's grade has then for the claim's date; an open claim's due stays live.
29	 * A claim records who opened it, and that user cannot settle it (four eyes). A claim bound by its
30	 * person's last statement keeps the figure it had then, and settling it fixes that figure. No claim
31	 * dated inside a closed period can be added, edited (to or from such a date) or change status. No
32	 * claim can be added or edited to a date after its person's retirement date. A clerk settles a claim
33	 * only when its figure is at or below the sheet's clerk limit (a claim with no figure is within any
34	 * limit); a steward settles any claim. A claim's live due is never below the sheet's floor. An
35	 * overdue claim's due gains a late charge on top of its figure (see {@link LateCharge}); a statement
36	 * binds only the figure under it, and settling fixes the charge into the settled due. A claim with
37	 * a negative amount is a correction: it is allowed only when it names, by number, a SETTLED claim
38	 * of the same person that it corrects. Its due has no floor and no late charge.
